with the black lightning DC launched his  first television show starring a black  superhero it's a milestone that's been a  long time coming but it's not the first  time Jefferson Pierce has managed to  break a long-standing barrier since  first appearing over 40 years ago he  served as a member of the Justice League  the outsiders a solo superhero and even  provided the DC Universe with a legacy  of heroic characters from his origins on  the page all the way to his current  status on the screen  he is the fascinating truth behind Black  Lightning DC's first black superhero the  first three decades of the superhero  genre were overwhelmingly White's but in  the late 60s that began to change at  Marvel Stan Lee and Jack Kirby  introduced a black panther and in 1973  Hero for Hire issue number one made Luke  Cage the first black superhero to  headline his own book at DC however  things moved a little more slowly  it wasn't until 1977 that Tony Isabella  a writer who had previously worked on  luke cage's adventures was hired to  create their first headlining black  superhero with isabella and artist  trevor von eden that year saw the debut  of black lightning Jefferson Pierce was  a gold medal winning Olympic decathlete  had returned to his old neighborhood in  Metropolis to work as a teacher when one  of his students was killed in an  altercation with a criminal organization  called the 100 Pierce decided to hit the  streets with a hi-tech costume to take  them on himself the black bomber the  hero that almost was Paul Platt  lightning was the idea that made it to  the page he wasn't DC's first thoughts  when it came to creating a black  superhero and as Isabella revealed on  his blog the original plan might have  been the worst idea in comics history  when Isabella was hired the editors  pitched him a character called the black  bomber with a hook being that he was  actually a white racist who turned into  a super-powered black man when he was  stressed out but neither personality  being aware of the other in other words  DC's first black superhero was not  actually going to be black and would  feature plenty of stereotypes including  a basketball uniform costume  fortunately for everyone concerned  Isabella taught them out of air 30 years  later though writer Dwayne McDuffie  well known for making satirical jabs at  the superhero genre worked him into a  story about an alternate reality where  everything had gone so wrong that the  brown bomber could be on the Justice  League The Outsiders the original run of  black lightning was canceled  after only 11 issues but if it's any  consolation it wasn't alone instead it  was a casualty of what fans have dubbed  the DC implosion all told a DC gave the  axe to twenty titles it was a move that  came so suddenly that most of those  series even had completely finished  stories including black lightning issue  12 that stayed in DC's archives until  they were published in a book called  cancelled comic cavalcade to secure the  copyrights five years later Black  Lightning got a second chance at stardom  when Batman quit the Justice League over  that teens reluctance to cause an  international incident he put together a  new team called The Outsiders the roster  included a handful of new characters  like katana who would go on to appear in  the Suicide Squad movie but it also  revived a few existing heroes including  Black Lightning over the course of the  outsiders five-year run everyone on the  team got a spotlight story highlighting  their mysterious handle tortured past  and Black Lightning was no exception in  his case it given up his costumed  identity and powers due to guilt over  the accidental death of a bystander  named - Trina Shelton whose family would  eventually return to get revenge I'm the  one who taught him to fly Black  Lightning had lighting his own show as a  new development but kress Williams isn't  actually the first actor to play the  character in live-action that honor  Believe It or Not goes to stand-up  comedian simbad who took a brief turn as  black lightning on a 1992 episode of  Saturday Night Live in a sketch set to  Superman's funeral tying into the van  current Death of Superman storyline cast  members like Chris Farley Dana Carvey  and Chris Rock appeared as Superman's  fellow heroes however Black Lightning  wasn't invited leading to an altercation  with Jimmy Olsen and by the way SNL  effects department that's not what  lightning looks like it's not the most  flattering portrayal for sure and the  part where Batman doesn't recognize his  old teammate is a real heartbreaker but  it is an interesting bit of pop-culture  prominence for a character who was still  pretty obscure for mainstream audiences  thunder lightning and grace with black  lightnings ties to the original roster  of the outsiders it's not surprising  that it have a connection to the team  when a new version was put together in  2003 in Outsiders issue 1 Judd Winick  and Tom Rainey introduced an disappears  aka Thunder the oldest of black  lightnings two daughters like her father  Anissa added some much-needed diversity  to the DC Universe when it  revealed that she was in a romantic  relationship with another member of the  outsiders crates joy her powers however  are completely different she can control  her density making her nearly  invulnerable in 2008 a nYSSA's younger  sister Jennifer originally introduced as  part of another alternate reality in the  pages of Kingdom Come joined her in the  mainstream continuity with powers that  was similar to her father's she took the  name lightning joining the Justice  League in 1979 the Black Lightning was  offered membership in the JLA but turned  it down becoming only the second  character ever to do so 30 years later  he finally accepted in 2006 Batman  Superman and Wonder Woman spent a story  arc literally sitting around the table  with a bunch of trading card style  photographs of their fellow heroes  debating who they should let into a  reformed League around that same time a  swamp zombie rebuilt a killer robot so  he could turn Red Tornado human and then  tear off his arm and ether yeah  that really happened but anyway that was  a MacGuffin to get plot lightning and  the rest to join up the Justice League  decided to just keep everyone who showed  up to fight the latest crisis and he  stuck around for the next few years  after DC we booted their universe in  2011 and then rebirthed it in 2016  he was south of the league and back to  being a solo hero the CW's Black  Lightning with the new Black Lightning  TV show The CW is pulling from the  entire history of the character in some  pretty interesting ways kress Williams  stars as Jefferson Pierce who still  works in education and his TV  incarnation he's the principal of a high  school in the city of Freeland who has  dedicated his tenure to helping kids and  eliminating violence like his earliest  Comics incarnation the CW's Black  Lightning is taking on the hundred and  Tobias whale and getting his costume and  equipment from Peter Gumby like the  version that showed up in Batman on the  outsiders he's been retired from super  heroics driven to give up on being a  vigilante by his aversion to violence  Anissa and Jennifer have already  appeared on the show both with the  powers they have in the comics and great  joy as arrows and hisses love interest  the only thing that could really  complete the saga is if they manage to  get an appearance by simbad thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to  [Music]
 

